-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/9ea6fe0c-103d-4a80-90d9-e2ab98e015fa
-- title:
--   Allocate and construct one shared reporting cell
-- statement:
--   Let $L=512hJ$, $k\le J$, and let subset functions $f,g$ be bounded by $B,C$ on sets of size at most $2hJ$. Their complete suffix-zeta tables and pointer cells lie before a five-cell record, which ends before free base $a$. Choose box cutoff $b\le512h(J-k)$ with $kh+b\le2hJ$, and a natural threshold $t$.
--
--   Assume the cell's complete allocation fits the space limit, its constant, radix-key, compact-address, sorted-index, value, and threshold word bounds hold, and its pair, width, and sorting depth bounds hold, with $S\le W$. Then
--   $$r=\operatorname{finish}(a,h,J,k,b),\qquad\text{the record and allocated catalog satisfy the exact entry contract}.$$
--   The entry comprises its metadata, sorted prefix index, pointer row, and signed suffix-box stages. Both source tables remain valid; memory below $a$ is preserved outside the record. Time is suffix downset-size computation plus entry construction plus $1500$.
--
--   This realizes the prescribed reporting-cell layout from its free address and dimensions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightSharedReportingCell.lean#L55-L201

